B.a84=new A.cm([B.hU,"These tactics wear down your prefrontal cortex, the seat of reasoning and willpower. As decision fatigue builds, it hands control to fast, impulsive shortcuts.",B.hT,"Repetition drills your motor cortex until swipes and taps run as automatic reflexes, so your thumb acts before your conscious intent can catch up.",B.hW,"Your parietal lobe builds spatial maps of interfaces so you can navigate on autopilot. Deceptive layouts plant traps exactly where that muscle memory expects safe buttons.",B.fl,"Pings and red dots trip your salience network, the brain's alarm circuit. Each one fires an orienting reflex you are wired never to ignore, urgent or not.",B.hS,"Unpredictable payoffs spike dopamine in your ventral striatum harder than expected ones ever could. It is the same reward loop that keeps gamblers pulling the lever.",B.hV,"Your social cognition network constantly tracks status and belonging. Being excluded or ignored registers in these circuits much like physical pain."],A.aA("cm<dr,o>"))
